## Summary

**App:** `data/WebTestBench/web_applications_hinted/WebTestBench_0054` — "TechSpecs KB", a single-route React/Vite knowledge base with three tabbed views.

**Screens & components annotated** (31 hinted elements):
- **Header tabs** (`Index.tsx`): `nav.documents` / `nav.graph` / `nav.favorites` as `navigation` with view targets, plus `nav.favorites.count` observable.
- **Document / Favorites lists** (`DocumentList.tsx`): search input (`state: search.query`, `controls` the list), module filter chips as toggles (`library.filter.module.*`, literal `selected` state), sort `<select>` with `data-semtag-options` mirroring its three options, empty-state observable, and a folded collection `<ns>.list` with items `<ns>.list.item.<doc-slug>` (navigation → `document.detail`) and per-item `.favorite` toggle controls.
- **Document viewer** (`DocumentViewer.tsx`): back navigation, title/last-updated/version observables, favorite toggle, `doc.sections` collection, `doc.related` collection with `doc.related.item.<slug>` navigation items.
- **Sections** (`DocumentSection.tsx`): each header as toggle with live `open`/`closed` state, expanded content observable, cross-doc links `doc.sections.item.<section>.link.<doc>` — the collapsed (non-functional) variant carries literal state `disabled`, describing the app's expand-to-access constraint without encoding test intent.
- **Knowledge graph** (`KnowledgeGraph.tsx`): zoom-in/out/reset actions sharing state key `graph.zoom` with the zoom-level observable, and SVG node collection `graph.nodes` / `graph.nodes.item.<doc-slug>`.
- **Toast** (`Toast.tsx`): `app.toast` observable + dismiss action. **NotFound**: home link.

**Id namespaces:** `nav`, `library`, `favorites`, `doc`, `graph`, `app`, `notfound`. The shared `DocumentList` derives its namespace from `showFavoritesOnly`, so the two views never collide (and only one renders at a time via `AnimatePresence mode="wait"`).

**Prop widening (the one permitted code change):** `FavoriteButton` and `EmptyState` now extend `React.ComponentProps` and spread `{...props}` so call sites pass `data-semtag-*` through; `FavoriteButton` additionally emits `data-semtag-state="on|off"` only when a semtag id was supplied.

**Left unhinted:** graph edges and legend (decorative/derivable), document-card metadata rows (slug already identifies items), the graph's drag/wheel pan surface (no discrete control to address).

